Package: maluos-vault
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-psycopg, python3-cryptography, python3-yaml,
 systemd (>= 250), maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.5)
Recommends: postgresql-18-maludb-core
Description: MaluOS secret vault: per-user credentials with a usage ledger
 A daemon on a Unix socket that keeps API keys, tokens and passwords for the
 humans and agents of a MaluOS host. The caller's identity is its Linux uid
 (peer credentials), mapped to a MaluDB principal; each principal owns a
 compartment, shared compartments are managed by operators, and grants give
 other principals or scopes use or read access. Values are AES-256-GCM
 blobs under a master key that systemd decrypts from a credential sealed to
 the TPM when the host has one. Every add, read, use, rotation, grant and
 denial is a row in the append-only ledger in the tenant schema.
 .
 Ships `maluctl secret` and the first-boot component that provisions the
 vault. Phase 6 slice 1 of the MaluOS inference gateway.
